<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
<h4 class="text-text-100 mt-2 -mb-1 text-base font-bold">✅ Idea 3: Year-based subfolders within each subject</h4>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Good idea in principle, but I'd suggest a slight refinement.</strong> Rather than putting JSON files inside a year folder, keep the year as a <strong>property of each question</strong> (which you already do with the schema field <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">source</code> / year) and store question banks as flat JSON files per subject. The reason: fetching 4 separate files (one per year) adds 4 network round-trips at session start. A single <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">ees-questions.json</code> per subject is faster and simpler.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">However, year-based <strong>image</strong> subfolders make sense because images are static assets:</p>
