<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Actually — I think I've spotted the real issue. Looking at the Worker code again, the <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">/questions</code> handler uses <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">CUBE_QUESTIONS</code> as a global variable name, but in Cloudflare Workers the KV binding is accessed via <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">env.CUBE_QUESTIONS</code>, not as a bare global.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Try this fix:</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">In <strong>Edit code</strong>, find this line in the <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">/questions</code> handler:</p>
