class="contents"><div data-is-streaming="false" class="group relative relative pb-3" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><h2 class="sr-only select-none">Claude responded: I can see your GitHub profile.</h2><div class="font-claude-response relative leading-[1.65rem] [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:bg-bg-000/50 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-0.5 [&amp;_pre&gt;div]:border-border-400 [&amp;_.ignore-pre-bg&gt;div]:bg-transparent [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.standard-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pl-2 [&amp;_.progressive-markdown_:is(p,blockquote,ul,ol,h1,h2,h3,h4,h5,h6)]:pr-8"><div><div class="standard-markdown grid-cols-1 grid [&amp;_&gt;_*]:min-w-0 gap-3 standard-markdown"><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">I can see your GitHub profile. The images need to go into your <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">allawrance.github.io</code> repository, but I don't see it listed in your popular repositories. Let me guide you:</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Step 1 — Find the right repository</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Click <strong>Repositories</strong> (top, shows 5) and look for one named <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">allawrance.github.io</code> — that's where your GitHub Pages site lives.</p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Step 2 — Create the folder and upload</strong></p>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal">Once inside <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">allawrance.github.io</code>:</p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>Add file → Upload files</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">In the upload area, you can drag and drop all 7 images at once</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Before committing, you need to set the path. GitHub won't let you create folders via upload directly, so instead:
<ul class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>Add file → Create new file</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">In the filename box type exactly: <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">EES/questions/images/2023/.gitkeep</code></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Scroll down, click <strong>Commit changes</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">This creates the folder structure</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal"><strong>Step 3 — Upload the images into that folder</strong></p>
<ol class="[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-decimal flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3">
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Navigate into <code class="bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">EES/questions/images/2023/</code></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>Add file → Upload files</strong></li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Drag all 7 PNGs in with their exact filenames</li>
<li class="font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2">Click <strong>Commit changes</strong></li>
</ol>
<hr class="border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5">
